rl":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103651","id":2943215140,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vbeYk","user":{"login":"camperotactico","id":22345650,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMzQ1NjUw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22345650?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/camperotactico","html_url":"https://github.com/camperotactico","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/camperotactico/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/camperotactico/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/camperotactico/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/camperotactico/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/camperotactico/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/camperotactico/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/camperotactico/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/camperotactico/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/camperotactico/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-05T08:21:06Z","updated_at":"2025-06-05T08:21:06Z","body":"I am also experiencing a similar issue, but I still have to do more testing before I discard the possibility that there is a bug in my code. \n\nI have been reading other issues similar to this, and I wonder if this is related to #96678.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2943215140/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2943333698","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103651#issuecomment-2943333698","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103651","id":2943333698,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vb7VC","user":{"login":"camperotactico","id":22345650,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMzQ1NjUw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22345650?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/camperotactico","html_url":"https://github.com/camperotactico","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/camperotactico/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/camperotactico/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/camperotactico/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/camperotactico/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/camperotactico/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/camperotactico/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/camperotactico/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/camperotactico/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/camperotactico/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-05T08:58:28Z","updated_at":"2025-06-05T08:58:28Z","body":"I was able to reproduce the issue I am having in my project, which I feel is related to this one, in a MRP.  The problem is shown when the character is moving diagonally towards the camera.\n\n[interpolation-bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20606604/interpolation-bug.zip)\n\nIn my case, not even `Exclusive Fullscreen`, or any of the `VSync` options seems to get rid of the issue. I tried this on both Fedora Linux 42 and MacOS 17.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2943333698/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2944206980","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103651#issuecomment-2944206980","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103651","id":2944206980,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vfQiE","user":{"login":"camperotactico","id":22345650,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMzQ1NjUw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22345650?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/camperotactico","html_url":"https://github.com/camperotactico","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/camperotactico/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/camperotactico/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/camperotactico/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/camperotactico/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/camperotactico/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/camperotactico/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/camperotactico/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/camperotactico/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/camperotactico/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-05T13:02:13Z","updated_at":"2025-06-05T13:02:13Z","body":"Hey, I think I figured out how to get rid of the jitter. I took @Thevgm01 MRP as an example, which you can find here:\n\n[jitter_mrp_fix.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20610820/jitter_mrp_fix.zip)\n\nThe changes I made to make the jitter go away are as follow:\n\n1.  Inside the `Project Settings`, I enabled `Physics Interpolation` and set `Physics Jitter Fix` to 0.0 **(This is important, as based on my testing, simply setting the `Physics Interpolation Mode` to `On` on a Node doesn't work on its own Even thought the  tooltip hints otherwise.)**\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/df50c38a-a0bf-421d-96a4-c7b081fded82)\n\n2. I used `follow_target.get_global_transform_interpolated().origin` in the `_process` method of the camera code, instead of `follow_target.global_position`\n\n3. Set the Camera3D `Physics Interpolation Mode` to `Off`, as enabling the physics interpolation globally in the project settings defaults any node that uses `Physics Interpolation Mode = Inherit` as `On`.\n\n\nIdeally, Just setting the `Physics Interpolation Mode` of any node should be enough to enable this functionality. Having to rely on enabling physics interpolation globally is problematic, since unless the root of the game is set to `Physics Interpolation Mode = Off` every single node will be interpolated by default.\n\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2944206980/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2949369234","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103651#issuecomment-2949369234","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103651","id":2949369234,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vy82S","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-06T14:03:07Z","updated_at":"2025-06-06T14:50:06Z","body":"Regarding the original MRP posted by @Thevgm01, this is not a bug. Change the script to use `_physics_process()` and enable **Physics Interpolation** in the project settings. Otherwise, any momentary frame drops or system-induced frametime variations (which is common on Windows in windowed mode) *will* cause visible jittering. I've tested this with various FPS caps and the MRP looks perfectly smooth with no jitter.\n\n> Inside the Project Settings, I enabled Physics Interpolation and set Physics Jitter Fix to 0.0\n\n**Physics Jitter Fix** is always considered to be `0.0` when physics interpolation is enabled, so you don't need to do that manually.\n\n> (This is important, as based on my testing, simply setting the Physics Interpolation Mode to On on a Node doesn't work on its own Even thought the tooltip hints otherwise.)\n\nI've opened a PR to clarify what the documentation actually tried to say 🙂 \n\n- https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107212","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2949369234/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":2,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]